    <h2>
        Hatha Yoga and Patanjali's Yoga
    </h2>

    <p>
        Hatha Yoga and the Yoga associated with Patanjali
        should not be treated as completely separate worlds.
    </p>

    <p>
        At the same time, their texts, terminology,
        practices and historical development are not identical.
    </p>

    <div class="card-grid">

        <article class="card">

            <h3>
                Patanjali
            </h3>

            <p>
                Gives a major place to ethical discipline,
                meditation, concentration and samadhi.
            </p>

        </article>


        <article class="card">

            <h3>
                Hatha Traditions
            </h3>

            <p>
                Give much greater textual attention to
                asana, pranayama, mudra, bandha and subtle-body
                practices.
            </p>

        </article>


        <article class="card">

            <h3>
                Shared Aim
            </h3>

            <p>
                Both can be understood as paths concerned
                with disciplined transformation and liberation,
                though their frameworks differ.
            </p>

        </article>

    </div>

</div>
