<!-- =====================================================
     MODERN HATHA YOGA
===================================================== -->

<section class="content-section alt-section">

```
<div class="container">

    <p class="eyebrow">
        THEN AND NOW
    </p>

    <h2>
        Classical Hatha Yoga and Modern Hatha Classes
    </h2>

    <p>
        The phrase “Hatha Yoga” is used very widely today.
    </p>

    <p>
        In many modern studios, Hatha can mean a slower,
        posture-based class with attention to alignment,
        breathing and relaxation.
    </p>

    <p>
        Classical Hatha Yoga literature is broader and includes
        practices and philosophical ideas that are not normally
        taught in a general fitness class.
    </p>

    <p>
        Understanding this difference helps students appreciate
        both modern Yoga education and the historical tradition.
    </p>

</div>
```

